        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "59b469cd-2c00-5434-909d-f4585935b47c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horton Foote, David Foster Wallace, Thomas C. Ryan, K.B. Gilden, Katya Gilden, Bert Gilden, William Shakespeare\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird, Tender Mercies, Hurry Sundown, Infinite Jest, Hamlet\n- Topics: screenwriting, television drama, novel pseudonyms, title origins\n\nFacts:\n- Horton Foote was an American playwright and screenwriter born on March 14, 1916, and he died on March 4, 2009.\n- Horton Foote was known for the screenplays for the 1962 film To Kill a Mockingbird and the 1983 film Tender Mercies, and for notable live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\n- David Foster Wallace was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing who was born on February 21, 1962, and died on September 12, 2008.\n- The screenplay for Hurry Sundown was written by Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan.\n- The screenplay for Hurry Sundown was based on the 1965 novel of the same title by K.B. Gilden.\n- K.B. Gilden was a pseudonym used by the married couple Katya Gilden and Bert Gilden.\n- The album Infinite Jest took its name from the David Foster Wallace novel Infinite Jest.\n- The title of David Foster Wallace's novel Infinite Jest was taken from a line in William Shakespeare's Hamlet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "434b0129-ecda-5578-a882-74f8f7f53a56",
        "text": "Page: Horton Foote. Sentence: Albert Horton Foote Jr. (March 14, 1916March 4, 2009) was an American playwright and screenwriter, perhaps best known for his screenplays for the 1962 film \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" and the 1983 film \"Tender Mercies\", and his notable live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\nPage: David Foster Wallace. Sentence: David Foster Wallace (February 21, 1962 – September 12, 2008) was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing.\nPage: Hurry Sundown (film). Sentence: The screenplay by Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan is based on the 1965 novel of the same title by K.B. Gilden, a pseudonym for married couple Katya and Bert Gilden.\nPage: Infinite Jest (album). Sentence: Its name is taken from the David Foster Wallace novel entitled \"Infinite Jest\", the title of which is in turn taken from a line in William Shakespeare's Hamlet.",
